    {
      "title": "High-level delegation visits Iran to try to avert flare-up with US and Israel",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/26/saudi-pakistani-turkish-delegation-iran-avert-flare-up-conflict-us",
      "description": "<p>Senior officials from Saudi Arabia, Pakistan and Turkey travel to Tehran as bellicose rhetoric heightens</p><p>High-level diplomatic delegations from Saudi Arabia, Turkey and Pakistan have travelled to Tehran in an attempt to prevent renewed fighting between Iran and the US and Israel <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/23/european-middle-eastern-ministers-summit-iran-us-israel\">as rhetoric sharpens on both sides</a>.</p><p>Security officials and diplomats at Monday’s meeting were expected to discuss how Iran could persuade the Houthis in Yemen to end their crippling missile and drone <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/22/us-diplomats-told-to-leave-saudi-arabia-amid-houthi-attacks\">attacks on infrastructure in Saudi Arabia</a>. With fighting raging across Yemen, the Houthis claimed to have closed Riyadh airport and inflicted heavy damage on the Saudi economy.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/26/saudi-pakistani-turkish-delegation-iran-avert-flare-up-conflict-us\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-26T14:03:06"
    },
    {
      "title": "Mecca defence alliance members in Tehran to defuse Iran-US, Yemen tensions",
