    },
    {
      "title": "Flurry of Diplomacy in Iran Amid Reports of U.S. and Israeli Plans to Renew War",
      "link": "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/26/world/middleeast/iran-war-new-attacks-diplomacy.html",
      "description": "Saudi Arabia, Turkey and Pakistan made a rare joint visit to Tehran amid reports that the U.S. and Israel were drawing up plans to renew their attacks on Iran.",
      "source_name": "NYT World News",
      "published": "2026-10-26T14:30:53"
    },
    {
      "title": "Top defence officials of Mecca pact countries hold talks in Tehran",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/saudi-pak-turkey-officials-meet-iranian-authorities-to-avert-renewed-war-126102600462_1.html",
      "description": "High-level delegations from Saudi Arabia, Pakistan and Turkiye were in Tehran on Monday for meetings with Iranian authorities to try to avert renewed fighting between Iran and Israel and the United States, two regional officials said.\nThe talks come as many in Iran are girding themselves for the possible return to all-out war, as Israeli and American leaders have been sharpening their threats ahead of pending elections in both countries, while Iranian leaders have remained defiant.\nSaudi Defence Minister Khalid bin Salman, Pakistan army chief Field Marshal Asim Munir and the head of Turkiye's intelligence service were to meet with Iran's top security officials and negotiators to push for a deal between Tehran and Washington.\nThe war in Yemen and strikes by Iranian-backed Houthi rebels against Saudi Arabia were topics also on the table, said the officials who spoke on condition of anonymity because they were not authorised to speak to reporters.\nAn Iranian official, also speaking on",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-26T08:11:56"
    },
    {
      "title": "Iran hosts regional powers for talks to prevent fresh escalation",
